Upstream's D-Bus policy grants the "cosmic-greeter" group access, but
the system account this package actually creates is "_cosmicgreeter"
(matching Void's leading-underscore convention for system users/groups).
Point the policy at the real group name, otherwise the greeter daemon
can't reach its own D-Bus service.

--- a/dbus/com.system76.CosmicGreeter.conf	2026-01-01 23:03:50.763553716 +0100
+++ b/dbus/com.system76.CosmicGreeter.conf	2026-01-01 23:04:14.723551461 +0100
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
           "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Bus Configuration 1.0//EN"
           "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/busconfig.dtd">
 <busconfig>
-    <policy group="cosmic-greeter">
+    <policy group="_cosmicgreeter">
         <allow send_destination="com.system76.CosmicGreeter"/>
         <allow receive_sender="com.system76.CosmicGreeter"/>
     </policy>
